A '''city''' was located on the [[planet]] [[Yerbana]] in the regions known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]], which was accessible from a single bridge that stretched across a chasm.<ref name="Old Friends" /> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TCWcanondates|709}}</ref> during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]] of the [[Clone Wars]], the [[city]] was occupied by a force of [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] [[battle droid]]s under the [[Commanding officer|command]] of an [[Unidentified super tactical droid (Yerbana)|ST-series super tactical droid]].<ref name="Old Friends" />

As its citizens began to suffer, the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[501st Legion]] and [[212th Attack Battalion]] launched an [[Battle of Yerbana|attack]] on the planet in an attempt to liberate the city under the leadership of [[Jedi General]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]]. As a result, the Republic was able to end the Confederacy's occupation of the city as well as claim control over the planet.<ref name="Old Friends" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Yerbana city was introduced in "[[Old Friends Not Forgotten]],"<ref name="Old Friends" /> the ninth episode of the seventh season of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series,<ref name="Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/old-friends-not-forgotten-episode-guide|text="Old Friends Not Forgotten" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> which is aired on [[April 17]], [[2020]].<ref name="dtcimedia">{{DisneyPlus|subdomain=press|url=disney-plus/star-wars-the-clone-wars/709|text=Episode 709 "Old Friends Not Forgotten"}}</ref>

